s","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Waiver approved allowing Army, Navy to play 13th game in 2027","description":"The waiver will allow Army and Navy to play 12 games apiece before the College Football Playoff selections are made and keep their rivalry game.","published":"2026-11-20T14:06:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50535192/waiver-approved-army-navy-13th-game-2027","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Jake Trotter","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"James Madison moving to American Conference in 2027","description":"James Madison is leaving the Sun Belt Conference for the American Conference a year earlier than planned, in 2027 rather than 2028.","published":"2026-11-19T21:30:55.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50534149/james-madison-moving-american-conference-2027","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4941011/john-nestor","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Nestor_(American_football)"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"John Nestor (American football)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Nestor_(American_football)","description":"American football player (born 2005)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:29Z","intro":"John Nestor (born May 13, 2005) is an American football cornerback for the Minnesota Golden Gophers. He previously played for the Iowa Hawkeyes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Nestor attended Marist High School in Chicago, Illinois. Coming out of high school, he was rated as a three-star recruit by 247Sports and committed to play college football for the Iowa Hawkeyes over offers from other schools such as Iowa State, Minnesota, Purdue, and Kansas."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"IOWA\nAs a freshman in 2023, Nestor played sparingly, but entered the 2024 season with an expanded role. He appeared in ten games that season, recording 14 tackles and a fumble recovery, after which he entered his name into the NCAA transfer portal.\n\nMINNESOTA\nNestor transferred to play for the Minnesota Golden Gophers. In week 2 of the 2025 season, he notched two interceptions, one of which he returned 29 yards for a touchdown, in a victory over Northwestern State. Nestor was named the Big Ten Defensive Player of the Week following a win over Wisconsin in the regular season finale, recording nine tackles with two being for a loss, two interceptions, and a fumble recovery."}]}}